From 78672c72efdd32a78a6e8aa49b75f142eab2f92b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luc3as <luc3as@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 16:45:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/25] Filter on the title and the seller, not just the price
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Vinted's text search matches descriptions as well as titles, so a search for
one model returns every listing that mentions it in passing. And the API says
who is selling — rating, review count, username — which is the difference
between a bargain and a gamble, but nothing acted on it.

A search can now require words in the title (all of them), match the title
against a regular expression, skip sellers below a rating or review count, and
skip named sellers. Available as CLI flags on `watch`, under "More filters" in
the dashboard, and stored in five new nullable columns (migration 0004) so
existing searches behave exactly as before.

filters.check() is now a pipeline of small gates rather than one long function;
same behaviour, same rejection reasons, easier to add the next one.
